<p>You have spent money on ads. You have posted on social media. You have sent emails. People are clicking through. But the leads are not coming in, and the sales are not happening. The problem almost certainly is not your traffic. It is where that traffic is landing.</p>

<p>Most small businesses send visitors to their homepage and hope for the best. A homepage is designed to give a general overview of your business. It has navigation, multiple pages, and a broad spread of information. That is fine for someone who already knows you. But for a new visitor arriving from an ad or a social post, all those options create confusion. Confusion kills conversions.</p>

<p>A landing page is different. It has one purpose and one action you want the visitor to take. Book a call. Download a guide. Sign up for a trial. Buy a product. Everything on the page exists to support that single goal. Nothing else.</p>

<p>If you want a deeper look at the differences between websites and funnels, our guide on <a href="/blog/website-vs-funnel">websites vs funnels</a> breaks it down in detail. But here, we are going to focus on the practical steps to build a landing page that actually converts.</p>

